{"kind":"artifact","text":"Exact clean head 6da2898ae6a9e985dd6cc3d180daa6d6fc7939f4 on request/serve-drop-acknowledge-flag removes the --acknowledge-trusted-processes gate from gs serve. Cut from main 0ec3618f; it fast-forwards.\n\nThe cmd/gs change is four deleted lines and nothing else: the set.Bool declaration at what was :1658, and the three-line refusal at :1667-1669. I verified independently that the flag had no consumer before deleting it, rather than trusting the request. The identifier acknowledgeTrustedProcesses occurred exactly twice in the tree, at its declaration and at the refusal that read it. It was a function-local *bool inside serveCommand that never escaped: not assigned to a field, a closure or a package variable, and never passed as an argument. The FlagSet it belonged to is created per call by flags() and returned only as a local, and no non-test Go file anywhere calls Lookup, Visit or VisitAll on a flag set, so nothing could read the value back by name either. The flag granted no authority and withheld none; it was a presence check.\n\nThe disclosure survives untouched, which is what makes this a safe deletion rather than the removal of a security statement. service.TrustedProcessPosture at internal/service/server.go:39 is unchanged, still printed unconditionally beside the listen address at cmd/gs/main.go:1716, and still carried as TrustBoundary in the status and summary payloads at server.go:177 and :251 with their assertions at server_test.go:229 and :269 passing under both test and race.\n\nThe tests: the refusal test TestServeRequiresExplicitTrustedProcessAcknowledgement is deleted outright rather than inverted, because with no refusal left an inverted version would only assert that Go's flag package parses arguments. Seven call sites across four tests and the startServing helper drop the argument and change nothing else — no assertion, timeout or control flow moved.\n\nONE CHANGE OUTSIDE THE REQUEST'S LISTED SCOPE, made deliberately and named here rather than buried. docs/reference/architecture.md:181 asserted that gs serve \"requires an explicit per-invocation acknowledgement\". The removal makes that false, and AGENTS.md requires the architecture page to match the head, so that clause now says the service discloses the posture on every start. Nothing else on the page moved and no layer contract changed.\n\nGates at this exact head, after go clean -testcache: make vet exit 0 with no findings; make build exit 0; make docs ok in 55.9s; make test exit 0 with 28 packages ok and zero failures; make race exit 0 with the same 28 packages and zero races, nothing cached; gofmt -l . empty; git status --porcelain empty. The single (cached) line in make test is internal/docset, whose cache entry was written by the make docs run minutes earlier in the same script at this same head after the cache was cleared, so it is not a pre-edit result.\n\nThe condition-3 gate passes: grep -rn 'acknowledge-trusted-processes' returns no match anywhere in the worktree, including .git. I also confirmed at the BASE commit, not only after my own deletions, that public_surface_test.go, layout_test.go, the Makefile, .github/ and spike/ contain no occurrence of the broader stem \"acknowledge\", so the public-surface and CI gates needed no change.\n\nThis artifact covers cmd/gs. Companion artifacts at docs and README.md stand at this same head and must be co-signed with it.","body":{"commit":"6da2898ae6a9e985dd6cc3d180daa6d6fc7939f4","path":"cmd/gs"}}